# locke over the corpus's shared atoms, written by phil/corpus from readings/locke/logic: not to be edited
atom	no_signs	we observe no footsteps in brutes of making use of general signs for universal ideas; they have no use of words or any other general signs
atom	abstract_brutes	brutes have the power of abstracting, or making general ideas
atom	man_general	man has general ideas
atom	distinction	the having of general ideas puts a perfect distinction betwixt man and brutes
P1	S2	no_signs	kind empirical
A1	-	abstract_brutes → ¬no_signs
C1	S2	¬abstract_brutes	from P1 A1
A2	-	man_general
A3	-	man_general ∧ ¬abstract_brutes → distinction
C	S1	¬abstract_brutes ∧ distinction	from C1 A2 A3
